    "id": "failed_order_lookup",
    "source": "bybit",
    "deviation": "AC-08",
    "note": "Expected reaction is the AC-08 deviation: a lookup that fails for any reason other than the unknown-order class keeps the order active, places and cancels nothing tied to it and retries up to the limit, then pauses. Before the adapter, a failed lookup could leave the order marked missing. Enforced by the engine's order-lookup rule (orders.resolve_order_state), not by the class table (ADR-0005).",
    "exception": {
      "kind": "pybit_invalid_request",
